  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), compute the weighted differences (i.e., expected values), and prefer the lottery with the more favorable mean difference — which is equivalent to preferring the higher expected value. However, the individual does not consider the expected values or differences from zero. Instead, the individual focuses solely on the probability of receiving money (25% vs. 20%) and prefers higher probability regardless of the monetary amount. This is a different reasoning process — one based on probability of success rather than on expected value or differences from a reference point. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason as described. The reasoning described in the verbal report is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
