  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to: (1) identify the reference value (500 Euros, from Lottery A), (2) compute the differences between outcomes and the reference value, and (3) evaluate the mean difference weighted by probabilities. The individual did not mention the reference value, nor did they compute or discuss differences (positive or negative) or their weighted average. Instead, the justification centers on emotional regret related to the possibility of receiving nothing, not on a comparative analysis of deviations from a reference. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The reasoning is qualitatively different — it is based on emotional regret and risk aversion, not on a formal calculation of mean differences from a reference value. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
